<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Cupul</h1><p class="st-meta">1441 CE – 1546 CE (approx.) · capital Saci</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A large Maya province of eastern Yucatán, including Chichen Itza, whose people led the Great Maya Revolt against Spanish rule in 1546.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Cupul formed after the collapse of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/league-of-mayapan">League of Mayapan</a> around 1441 under the Cupul lineage. It covered a large area of east-central Yucatán, including the ruins of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chichen-itza">Chichen Itza</a>, with its main town at Saci, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valladolid-yucatan">Valladolid</a> now stands.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The province was governed by lords of the Cupul lineage, who appear to have shared power among several branches rather than recognising one supreme ruler. Its people farmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maize">maize</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> and honey. The Cupul resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-de-montejo">Montejo</a>'s first invasions in the late 1520s and early 1530s, forcing him to abandon a base at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chichen-itza">Chichen Itza</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1545 the Spanish founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valladolid-yucatan">Valladolid</a> at Saci. In 1546 the Cupul rose with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sotuta">Sotuta</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-maya-revolt">Great Maya Revolt</a>, killing Spaniards and their allies, but were crushed in 1547. The province became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-yucatan">Province of Yucatán</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/cupul.jpg" alt="Cupul" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Cacicazgos_mayas.jpg: Jaontiveros Mexico_States_blank_map.svg: Sémhur derivative work: ecelan (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cacicazgos_mayas_-_es.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1441 CE – 1546 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Saci</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Maya religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Yucatec Maya</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Cupul province</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1494&amp;focus=cupul" aria-label="Cupul on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="1945 1294 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Cupul lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2591 1670h0M4910 989h0M2590 1658h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2265 1550h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M2265 1550h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Mexico. <a href="/atlas?year=1494&amp;focus=cupul">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
